    "scope": "Within the boundary: US executive branch deliberations and proposed diesel export limits; behaviour and capacities of US refiners; diesel and crude physical flows (inventories, exports/imports, storage levels); tanker/shipping constraints and costs; price formation in diesel and crude futures and physical markets; European and Asian diesel demand and emergency measures; industry and business lobbying; near-term diplomatic developments related to the Iran conflict that affect supply.",
    "super_system": "Global energy security and geopolitics (crude oil and refined fuels markets embedded in international trade and diplomatic relations)",
    "adjacent_subsystems": [
      "International maritime shipping and maritime security (tankers, S2S transfers, insurance)",
      "European domestic energy policy and politics (fuel subsidies, taxation, storage mandates, electoral risks)",
      "US domestic politics and trade policy (executive decisions, industry lobbying, campaign linkages)",
      "Global refining and petroleum product logistics (refinery runs, blending, bunker and road fuel distribution)"
    ],
    "evidence_headlines": [
